<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Muslim ibn Quraysh</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1085">1085</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Muslim ibn <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quraysh">Quraysh</a>, called <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sharaf-al-dawla">Sharaf al-Dawla</a>, was the Uqaylid emir of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mosul">Mosul</a> from 1061 to 1085 and one of the leading Arab princes of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> under Seljuk overlordship. He took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aleppo">Aleppo</a> in 1080 and held <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harran">Harran</a> and other towns of the Jazira. He was killed in 1085 fighting Sulayman ibn <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qutalmish">Qutalmish</a>, the Seljuk ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>, near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antioch">Antioch</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/muslim-ibn-quraysh.jpg" alt="Muslim ibn Quraysh" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mustafa Wahhudi · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Muhammad_Al-Durri_Shrine.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
